/* Terminus Font, as glyph data.
 *
 * Not ours, and in a file of its own for that reason. The manifest gives every
 * file exactly one licence, and a file holding both somebody else's font and
 * our own code cannot honestly have one - so the font is here, under the SIL
 * Open Font Licence 1.1, and the code that looks glyphs up is next door under
 * ours. See LICENSE-MANIFEST and third-party/terminus-font/.
 *
 * Copyright (C) 2020 Dimitar Toshkov Zhekov, with Reserved Font Name
 * "Terminus Font". Nothing here is called Terminus: this is a converted
 * subset, which OFL counts as a modification, and a modified version may not
 * carry the reserved name.
 *
 * An earlier version of this file carried a Cyrillic alphabet drawn by hand
 * for this project. It looked like what it was - fifty letters drawn one at a
 * time with no common grid, so the height wandered and words came out as a
 * smear. Type design is a craft.
 *
 * Generated from ter-u16n.psf. Laid out on code page 437, which is what a
 * DOS-looking system draws its frames with; anything past 255 is found by code
 * point in the second table.
 */

